-[15px] leading-snug py-1 pl-2.5 -ml-2.5 border-l-[3px] transition-colors border-transparent text-ink-soft hover:text-ink">The shot model (xG)</button></li><li><button type="button" class="w-full text-left text-[15px] leading-snug py-1 pl-2.5 -ml-2.5 border-l-[3px] transition-colors border-transparent text-ink-soft hover:text-ink">Does it predict goals?</button></li><li><button type="button" class="w-full text-left text-[15px] leading-snug py-1 pl-2.5 -ml-2.5 border-l-[3px] transition-colors border-transparent text-ink-soft hover:text-ink">The coefficients</button></li><li><button type="button" class="w-full text-left text-[15px] leading-snug py-1 pl-2.5 -ml-2.5 border-l-[3px] transition-colors border-transparent text-ink-soft hover:text-ink">Blocked shots</button></li></ul></div></div><div class=""><div class="mb-3 last:mb-0"><div class="dateline pb-1.5 mb-1 border-b border-rule">Player value</div><ul><li><button type="button" class="w-full text-left text-[15px] leading-snug py-1 pl-2.5 -ml-2.5 border-l-[3px] transition-colors border-transparent text-ink-soft hover:text-ink">Net Rating</button></li><li><button type="button" class="w-full text-left text-[15px] leading-snug py-1 pl-2.5 -ml-2.5 border-l-[3px] transition-colors border-transparent text-ink-soft hover:text-ink">The Estimated Net Rating</button></li><li><button type="button" class="w-full text-left text-[15px] leading-snug py-1 pl-2.5 -ml-2.5 border-l-[3px] transition-colors border-transparent text-ink-soft hover:text-ink">iWPA: who moved the game</button></li><li><button type="button" class="w-full text-left text-[15px] leading-snug py-1 pl-2.5 -ml-2.5 border-l-[3px] transition-colors border-transparent text-ink-soft hover:text-ink">GS+: the game card‚Äôs number</button></li><li><button type="button" class="w-full text-left text-[15px] leading-snug py-1 pl-2.5 -ml-2.5 border-l-[3px] transition-colors border-accent text-ink font-semibold" aria-current="page">Power-play roles</button></li></ul></div></div><div class="col-span-2 sm:col-span-1 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-1 gap-x-5"><div class="mb-3 last:mb-0"><div class="dateline pb-1.5 mb-1 border-b border-rule">Tracking data</div><ul><li><button type="button" class="w-full text-left text-[15px] leading-snug py-1 pl-2.5 -ml-2.5 border-l-[3px] transition-colors border-transparent text-ink-soft hover:text-ink">All Three Zones, estimated</button></li></ul></div><div class="mb-3 last:mb-0"><div class="dateline pb-1.5 mb-1 border-b border-rule">Goaltending</div><ul><li><button type="button" class="w-full text-left text-[15px] leading-snug py-1 pl-2.5 -ml-2.5 border-l-[3px] transition-colors border-transparent text-ink-soft hover:text-ink">The next-season forecast</button></li></ul></div><div class="mb-3 last:mb-0"><div class="dateline pb-1.5 mb-1 border-b border-rule">Badges</div><ul><li><button type="button" class="w-full text-left text-[15px] leading-snug py-1 pl-2.5 -ml-2.5 border-l-[3px] transition-colors border-transparent text-ink-soft hover:text-ink">Skills, usage, and how they relate</button></li></ul></div><div class="mb-3 last:mb-0"><div class="dateline pb-1.5 mb-1 border-b border-rule">Archive</div><ul><li><button type="button" class="w-full text-left text-[15px] leading-snug py-1 pl-2.5 -ml-2.5 border-l-[3px] transition-colors border-transparent text-ink-soft hover:text-ink">Retired metrics</button></li></ul></div></div></div></nav><article id="pp-roles-writeup" class="prose-paper"><header class="mb-10"><div class="dateline">Writeups ¬∑ Player roles ¬∑ The power play</div><h1 class="font-serif text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-2 mb-3">Power-play roles: who stands where</h1><p class="deck">Every power-play unit puts five skaters in five places, and the play-by-play never says which is which. We read it off where their events happen and publish the split as percentages.</p><aside class="mt-4 border-l-2 border-rule pl-3 text-sm text-ink-soft"><span class="font-semibold">Editor's note:</span> This article was AI-generated, for transparency on methodology. A human writer has not yet edited it.</aside></header><nav class="border border-rule rounded-sm p-4 mb-12 bg-paper"><div class="dateline mb-2">Contents</div><ol class="list-decimal ml-5 space-y-1 text-sm"><li><a href="#ppr-what" class="text-accent hover:underline">What a slot is</a></li><li><a href="#ppr-how" class="text-accent hover:underline">How it is read</a></li><li><a href="#ppr-left-out" class="text-accent hover:underline">What we left out, and why</a></li><li><a href="#ppr-accuracy" class="text-accent hover:underline">How often it is right</a></li><li><a href="#ppr-gates" class="text-accent hover:underline">The bar we set, and missed</a></li><li><a href="#ppr-limits" class="text-accent hover:underline">What it cannot do</a></li></ol></nav><section id="ppr-what" class="mb-12 scroll-mt-20"><div class="dateline section-rule">What a slot is</div><h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-1 mb-4">What a slot is</h2><div class="space-y-3 text-ink leading-relaxed"><p class="drop-cap">Most NHL power plays set up as a 1-3-1. One skater works the blue line: the point. Two work the half-walls, one on each side, usually the shooters and passers the unit is built around. One sits in the middle of the zone, between the circles: the bumper. One lives at the net, screening and tipping: the net-front. Five skaters, five slots, one of each.</p><p>Post Hockey shows this on each team's page, unit by unit. For a team's most-used five-man power-play units, the grid gives each player's share of the unit's five-on-four time in each slot. Every row adds to 100%, and so does every column: within a unit each slot is somebody's, all of the time. The rink seats the five in the unit's most likely arrangement; a player under half in his seat rotates, and the grid shows where. Left and right are the attacker's, looking at the net: the left half-wall is the one Alex Ovechkin shoots from.</p></div></section><section id="ppr-how" class="mb-12 scroll-mt-20"><div class="dateline section-rule">How it is read</div><h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-1 mb-4">How it is read</h2><div class="space-y-3 text-ink leading-relaxed"><p>Nothing in the NHL's data records where a player stands. It records where each player's events happen: shots that reach the net or miss it, shots that are blocked (only the angle survives those, since the coordinates are the blocker's), giveaways and takeaways in the offensive zone, penalties drawn and hits taken in the opponent's end. Each slot has its own map of where those events come from and how often they happen, and the maps are fitted, not drawn by us: we seeded them with five boxes on the rink and let the data move them.</p><p>The read is joint. A unit holds exactly one of each slot, so all five skaters on the ice are placed at once, over every way of assigning five players to five slots. That is what separates the bumper from the net-front when their rebounds land in the same place, and the point from a half-wall man walking down the wall: if the point is obviously the defenceman, the other four have to be somewhere else. The model is fitted on every five-on-four stretch from 2021-22 on, and a player's previous season is the starting guess for the next. A unit is shown when its five played at least five minutes of five-on-four together, up to three per team-season, and its grid is the fit's own reading of those minutes, pooled.</p></div></section><section id="ppr-left-out" class="mb-12 scroll-mt-20"><div class="dateline section-rule">What we left out, and why</div><h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-1 mb-4">What we left out, and why</h2><div class="space-y-3 text-ink leading-relaxed"><p>Faceoffs and assists are not inputs. Both were in the first version, and both say who a player is rather than where the player is. The centre takes the draw wherever the centre then sets up, so with faceoffs in, the model decided that ‚Äúbumper‚Äù meant ‚Äúthe centre‚Äù, and every first-unit centre came out as the bumper, including the ones who run the half-wall. An assist records that a player passed, not from where. With both removed, the centres went back to where they actually play, and the score against hand-labelled units went up. Neither appears anywhere in the number.</p></div></section><section id="ppr-accuracy" class="mb-12 scroll-mt-20"><div class="dateline section-rule">How often it is right</div><h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-1 mb-4">How often it is right</h2><div class="space-y-3 text-ink leading-relaxed"><p>We hand-labelled the first power-play unit of every team we could in 2024-25, before fitting anything: who played the point, the half-walls, the bumper and the net. Half of those teams were used to choose the two settings we were unsure of. The other half, BUF, DAL, EDM, LAK, MTL, NSH, STL, TOR, VGK, WSH, was scored once, at the end. The table compares the model's top slot for each labelled player with the label, alongside three ways of guessing without it.</p><table class="text-sm border border-rule my-4 w-full max-w-xl"><thead><tr class="border-b border-rule-strong text-ink-faint text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider"><th class="px-3 py-2 text-left font-medium">Top slot right, of five</th><th class="px-3 py-2 text-right font-medium">Held-out half (50)</th><th class="px-3 py-2 text-right font-medium">All labelled (109)</th></tr></thead><tbody class="tabular-nums"><tr class="border-b border-rule font-semibold"><td class="px-3 py-1.5">The model</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">72%</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">70%</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-rule"><td class="px-3 py-1.5">Where most of the player's shots came from</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">66%</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">67%</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-rule"><td class="px-3 py-1.5">Position only: defencemen at the point</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">38%</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">39%</td></tr><tr><td class="px-3 py-1.5">A random slot</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">20%</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">20%</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The model's confidence means something. Split by how large a player's top share is:</p><table class="text-sm border border-rule my-4 w-full max-w-xl"><thead><tr class="border-b border-rule-strong text-ink-faint text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider"><th class="px-3 py-2 text-left font-medium">Top share</th><th class="px-3 py-2 text-right font-medium">Held-out half</th><th class="px-3 py-2 text-right font-medium">All labelled</th></tr></thead><tbody class="tabular-nums"><tr class="border-b border-rule last:border-0"><td class="px-3 py-1.5">top share 0.7 or more</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">95% <span class="text-ink-faint">(19 of 20)</span></td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">95% <span class="text-ink-faint">(37 of 39)</span></td></tr><tr class="border-b border-rule last:border-0"><td class="px-3 py-1.5">0.5 to 0.7</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">67% <span class="text-ink-faint">(14 of 21)</span></td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">64% <span class="text-ink-faint">(27 of 42)</span></td></tr><tr class="border-b border-rule last:border-0"><td class="px-3 py-1.5">under 0.5 (shown as Mixed role)</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">33% <span class="text-ink-faint">(3 of 9)</span></td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">43% <span class="text-ink-faint">(12 of 28)</span></td></tr></tbody></table><p>And by slot, over all labelled players: how many of a slot's labelled players the model found (recall), and how many of the players it put there belong there (precision).</p><table class="text-sm border border-rule my-4 w-full max-w-xl"><thead><tr class="border-b border-rule-strong text-ink-faint text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider"><th class="px-3 py-2 text-left font-medium">Slot</th><th class="px-3 py-2 text-right font-medium">Labelled</th><th class="px-3 py-2 text-right font-medium">Recall</th><th class="px-3 py-2 text-right font-medium">Precision</th></tr></thead><tbody class="tabular-nums"><tr class="border-b border-rule last:border-0"><td class="px-3 py-1.5">Net-front</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">22</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">77%</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">74%</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-rule last:border-0"><td class="px-3 py-1.5">Bumper</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">23</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">52%</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">60%</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-rule last:border-0"><td class="px-3 py-1.5">Point</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">23</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">91%</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">95%</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-rule last:border-0"><td class="px-3 py-1.5">Left half-wall</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">21</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">67%</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">64%</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-rule last:border-0"><td class="px-3 py-1.5">Right half-wall</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">20</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">60%</td><td class="px-3 py-1.5 text-right">55%</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section id="ppr-gates" class="mb-12 scroll-mt-20"><div class="dateline section-rule">The bar we set, and missed</div><h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-1 mb-4">The bar we set, and missed</h2><div class="space-y-3 text-ink leading-relaxed"><p>Before fitting anything we wrote down what the model had to clear before we would publish it: the right top slot for at least 90% of labelled net-front and point players, and the right side of the bumper-or-half-wall line for at least 75%. On the held-out half it managed 85% of 20 and 67% of 30. It missed both.</p><p>We published it anyway, and said so here. It first ran as a panel on every player page; in October we moved it to team pages, unit by unit, because one label per player claims more than the model can back. The point and the half-walls are read well, and the percentages are honest about doubt (the confidence table above is the evidence). What does not clear the bar is the split between bumper and net-front, and which half-wall a player works. The unit grid shows that doubt rather than hiding it in a single word.</p></div></section><section id="ppr-limits" class="mb-12 scroll-mt-20"><div class="dateline section-rule">What it cannot do</div><h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mt-1 mb-4">What it cannot do</h2><div class="space-y-3 text-ink leading-relaxed"><ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2"><li><strong>The bumper is the weakest slot.</strong> Its events overlap the net-front's in the low slot, and some units rotate the two. Several of the misses above are a bumper read as a net-front or the other way round, some of them players who alternate between the two.</li><li><strong>The side is often swapped.</strong> The half-wall share is reliable as a pair; which wall is less so. A one-timer from the right circle and a pass across from the left leave similar traces.</li><li><strong>Events are not positions.</strong> A net-front player who steps out for a rebound shoots from the slot. The model reads where events cluster, not where a player stands between them.</li><li><strong>Breakouts are invisible.</strong> Nothing in the data shows what happens between a faceoff and a shot, so drop passes and entries are not part of this. The roles describe the offensive-zone setup only.</li><li><strong>Not every power play is a 1-3-1.</strong> An umbrella (two low, three high) still gets five slots from the model, the closest fit it can find.</li></ul></div></section></article></div><!--/$--><!--$--><!--/$--></main><aside aria-label="Support Post Hockey" class="mt-16 -mb-16 border-t border-rule bg-paper"><p class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-2.5 text-center text-sm text-ink-soft">Want to help Post Hockey pay for server costs?<!-- --> <a class="text-accent font-medium underline underline-offset-2 hover:opacity-80" href="/subscribe">Consider supporting here.</a></p></aside><footer class="border-t border-rule-strong mt-16"><div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-6 flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-4 text-sm"><span class="dateline">Post Hockey ¬∑ <!-- -->2026</span><nav class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-1 font-serif text-ink-soft"><a class="hover:text-accent transition-colors" href="/articles">Articles</a><a class="hover:text-accent transition-colors" href="/about">About</a><a class="hover:text-accent transition-colors" href="/glossary">Glossary &amp; Methods</a><a class="hover:text-accent transition-colors" href="/acknowledgements">Acknowledgements</a><a class="hover:text-accent transition-colors" href="/changelog">Changelog</a><a class="hover:text-accent transition-colors" href="/contribute">Submit research</a><a class="hover:text-accent transition-colors" href="/terms">Terms of Use</a></nav></div></footer><!--$--><!--/$--><script>requestAnimationFrame(function(){$RT=performance.now()});</script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/webpack-4de00440a42f40d7.js?dpl=dpl_7QxytHnTqYpcuVQeFovewbGBjCrk" id="_R_" async=""></script><script>$RB=[];$RV=function(a){$RT=performance.now();for(var b=0;b<a.length;b+=2){var c=a[b],e=a[b+1];null!==e.parentNode&&e.parentNode.removeChild(e);var f=c.parentNode;if(f){var g=c.previousSibling,h=0;do{if(c&&8===c.nodeType){var d=c.data;if("/$"===d||"/&"===d)if(0===h)break;else h--;else"$"!==d&&"$?"!==d&&"$~"!==d&&"$!"!==d&&"&"!==d||h++}d=c.nextSibling;f.removeChild(c);c=d}while(c);for(;e.firstChild;)f.insertBefore(e.firstChild,c);g.data="$";g._reactRetry&&requestAnimationFrame(g._reactRetry)}}a.length=0};
