s he went over 22 mph."+w+v}},{key:"edge_sprints",label:"Sprints",group:"Speed bursts",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,strengthAware:!1,toiKey:"edge_toi_seconds",gpKey:"edge_gp",help:{text:"Times he went over 18 mph: the three burst columns added up, so how often he skates hard, which is as much a role as a skating figure."+w+v}},{key:"edge_burst_mu",label:"Typical burst",group:"Speed",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,strengthAware:!1,kind:"pct",format:x,title:(e,t)=>(function(e){let t=e.edge_burst_mu,s=e.edge_burst_mu_sd,a=e.edge_burst_sigma;if(null==t)return;let o=[];if(o.push("".concat(t.toFixed(1)," mph")),null!=s&&o.push("80% range ".concat((0,i.mK)(t+1.2816*s).toFixed(2),"-").concat((0,i.mK)(t-1.2816*s).toFixed(2)," s")),null!=a){let t="D"===e.position?"every defenceman":"every forward";o.push("burst spread ".concat(a.toFixed(1)," mph, shared by ").concat(t," (fitted on the league, not on him)"))}return o.join("; ")||void 0})(t),help:{text:"His most common burst peak: where his fitted burst distribution peaks, read from his bins and ten fastest speeds and shrunk toward his position. Inferred, since EDGE sees only the part over 18 mph, so it can sit below 18 mph. Hover a cell for the mph and the 80% range. Every forward's bursts share one spread around it, and every defenceman's another (the scale, fitted on the league, not on him); the hover gives it."+y+P+w}},{key:"edge_burst_speed",label:"Hourly burst",group:"Speed",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,strengthAware:!1,kind:"pct",format:x,title:e=>null!=e?"".concat(e.toFixed(1)," mph"):void 0,help:{text:"The speed he reaches about once an hour of ice time: where his fitted burst curve (bins and ten fastest speeds, drawn on his player page) crosses one burst per 60. Steadier year to year than the season max, which is one reading. Hover a cell for the mph."+y+P+w}},{key:"edge_burst_speed_pct",label:"Burst pctile",group:"Speed",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,strengthAware:!1,kind:"pct",format:b,help:{text:"Where his hourly burst ranks among skaters at his position that season, 0-100. A rank, not a count."+P+w}},{key:"edge_max_speed",label:"Max speed",group:"Speed",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,strengthAware:!1,kind:"pct",format:k,help:{text:"His top skating speed of the season, miles per hour. A maximum, not a count."+P+w}},{key:"edge_oz_pct",label:"OZ%",group:"Zone time",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"pct",format:b,help:{text:"Share of his on-ice time spent in the offensive zone, 0 to 100."+S+T}},{key:"edge_nz_pct",label:"NZ%",group:"Zone time",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"pct",format:b,help:{text:"Share of his on-ice time spent in the neutral zone, 0 to 100."+S+T}},{key:"edge_dz_pct",label:"DZ%",group:"Zone time",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"pct",format:b,help:{text:"Share of his on-ice time spent in the defensive zone, 0 to 100."+S+T}},{key:"edge_oz_start_pct",label:"OZ start %",group:"Zone time",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"pct",format:b,help:{text:"Share of his zone starts that were in the offensive zone, as NHL EDGE counts them. EDGE does not split starts by strength, so this is every situation whatever the filter. A share, so the Total / Per 60 / Per 84 toggle leaves it alone. "+"Regular season; blank under ".concat(G," minutes at the filter's strength.")}},{key:"edge_xgf_oz60",label:"xGF(sh)/60 OZ",group:"Zone rates",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"pct",format:k,help:{text:"xGF(sh)/60 OZ = 60 \xd7 on-ice xGF(sh) \xf7 (OZ% \xd7 TOI): the shooter-adjusted expected goals for while he was on, per 60 minutes his team spent in the offensive zone. How dangerous his offensive-zone time was, apart from how much of it he got."+T+j}},{key:"edge_xga_dz60",label:"xGA(sh)/60 DZ",group:"Zone rates",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"pct",format:k,help:{text:"xGA(sh)/60 DZ = 60 \xd7 on-ice xGA(sh) \xf7 (DZ% \xd7 TOI): the shooter-adjusted expected goals against while he was on, per 60 minutes in the defensive zone. Lower is better."+T+j}}],F=[{key:"finisher",name:"Finisher",kind:"skill",sentence:"Scores more than his shots should."},{key:"forcefield",name:"Forcefield",kind:"skill",sentence:"Nothing gets through (defencemen)."},{key:"wall",name:"Wall",kind:"skill",sentence:"Holds the blue line (defencemen), from All Three Zones tracking."},{key:"slingshot",name:"Boomerang",kind:"skill",sentence:"Turns the dumps he goes back for into clean exits (defencemen): the share of his retrieval attempts that led straight to an exit, from All Three Zones tracking."},{key:"netfront",name:"Netfront",kind:"skill",sentence:"Scores from the blue paint (forwards)."},{key:"playmaker",name:"Playmaker",kind:"skill",sentence:"Makes the shot before the shot, from All Three Zones tracking."},{key:"transporter",name:"Transporter",kind:"skill",sentence:"Carries the puck in, from All Three Zones tracking."},{key:"motor",name:"Motor",kind:"skill",sentence:"Never stops working (forwards), from All Three Zones tracking."},{key:"speedster",name:"Speedster",kind:"skill",sentence:"Fast: the top speed he reaches about once an hour, read as blue line to blue line time, from NHL EDGE."},{key:"hardminutes",name:"Hard Minutes",kind:"role",sentence:"Sent out against the other side's best, with less help, and on the kill."},{key:"scorer",name:"Scorer",kind:"outcome",sentence:"Puts the puck in (forwards)."},{key:"ledger",name:"Ledger",kind:"outcome",sentence:"What the scoreboard did with him out there."},{key:"muncher",name:"Minute Muncher",kind:"role",sentence:"Plays the most."},{key:"spearhead",name:"Spearhead",kind:"role",sentence:"Sent out to attack."},{key:"anchor",name:"Sentry",kind:"role",sentence:"Sent out to defend."},{key:"enforcer",name:"Enforcer",kind:"role",sentence:"The heavy."},{key:"beanbag",name:"Beanbag",kind:"skill",sentence:"Stands in the lane: blocks the attempts against him."},{key:"ironman",name:"Iron Man",kind:"role",sentence:"Never out of the lineup."},{key:"quickdraw",name:"Quick Draw",kind:"skill",sentence:"Wins the draw that matters (centres)."}],D={skill:"Skill badges",role:"Role badges",outcome:"Outcome badges"},O={skill:0,role:1,outcome:2},z=[...F].sort((e,t)=>O[e.kind]-O[t.kind]).map(e=>({key:"badge_p_".concat(e.key),label:e.name,group:D[e.kind],sortable:!0,defaultVisible:"skill"===e.kind,kind:"pct",format:b,strengthAware:!1,help:{text:"".concat(e.name,": ").concat(e.sentence).concat(" The number is the chance, 0 to 100, that he is in the top tenth of his position group (forwards or defencemen) this season: the probability the badge pages publish. Whole regular season only."),href:"/glossary?tab=writeups&writeup=badges"}})),H=" A share, so the rate toggle leaves it alone. Counted in the situations CA and xGA(sh) are: at All, pulled-goalie play is out, so Blk here can be a few fewer than the Blk column. The block values come from the release-point model, which is accepted, not validated (see the blocked-shots writeup). Regular season, 2023-24 on. Ordered by this column, the table asks for 20 games played unless you set your own floors.",K=[{key:"blk_pct_ca",label:"Blk% of CA",group:"Blocked shots",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"pct",format:b,help:{text:"Blk% of CA = 100 \xd7 his blocks \xf7 on-ice CA. CA counts every opponent attempt while he was on the ice, blocked ones included, so his own blocks are inside it."+H,href:"/glossary?tab=writeups&writeup=blocked-shots"}},{key:"blk_xg_pct",label:"Blk xG%",group:"Blocked shots",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"pct",format:b,help:{text:"Blk xG% = 100 \xd7 Blk xG(sh) \xf7 (on-ice xGA(sh) + On-ice Blk xGA(sh)). xGA(sh) counts unblocked attempts only, so the blocked attempts' xG(sh) is added back to make the whole of the danger against him."+H,href:"/glossary?tab=writeups&writeup=blocked-shots"}},{key:"oi_blocked_xga_sh",label:"On-ice Blk xGA(sh)",group:"Blocked shots",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,format:k,help:{text:"The Blk xG(sh) of every opponent attempt his team blocked while he was on the ice, his own blocks included: the blocked part of the danger against him, which xGA(sh) leaves out. Each block's value is stored per blocker, game and situation, not per shot, so a teammate's block is valued at the average of that blocker's blocks in that game and situation; where he was on for all of them, as he usually is, the sum is exact. Regular season, 2023-24 on.",href:"/glossary?tab=writeups&writeup=blocked-shots"}}],Z=" A share, so the Total / Per 60 / Per 84 toggle leaves it alone. Follows the strength filter, the regular season / playoffs choice and the date window. Blank on the separate team rows of a player traded mid-season, which are not counted per stint.",B="Tips and deflections (the two shot types merged, because scorers do not code the split consistently) among his unblocked attempts: goals, shots on goal and misses. Blocked shots carry no shot type, so they are out of the count and the base. Before 2022-23 the rink's scorer shaped the coding, about 15% from rink to rink, so compare early seasons with care. The net-front man's stat.",I="Rebound attempts: his attempts, blocked ones included, made within three seconds of his team's previous unblocked attempt. 2022-23 on only: before then the timestamps were set by each rink's scorer and the count would be a rink effect, so earlier seasons read \"-\". The league rate has climbed every season since 2022-23, so compare within a season.",R=[{key:"defl",label:"Defl",group:"Deflections",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,help:{text:"Defl = his tipped or deflected unblocked attempts. "+B+" A count: the rate toggle turns it into Per 60 or Per 84."}},{key:"defl_pct",label:"Defl%",group:"Deflections",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"pct",format:b,help:{text:"Defl% = 100 \xd7 Defl \xf7 his unblocked attempts. "+B+Z}},{key:"reb",label:"Reb",group:"Rebounds",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,help:{text:"Reb = his rebound attempts. "+I+" A count: the rate toggle turns it into Per 60 or Per 84."}},{key:"reb_pct",label:"Reb%",group:"Rebounds",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"pct",format:b,help:{text:"Reb% = 100 \xd7 Reb \xf7 his attempts (blocked ones included). "+I+Z}},{key:"usage_pct",label:"Usage%",group:"Usage",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"pct",format:b,help:{text:"Usage% = 100 \xd7 his shot attempts \xf7 his team's shot attempts while he was on the ice: the share of his unit's attempts that he took himself. Attempts only, giveaways are not in it. It reads the CF column for the team side, so at All, pulled-goalie play is out of both sides."+Z}}],N=" Regular season, every situation, so the strength filter does not change it, and Per 60 is per 60 of his minutes in every situation and Per 84 is per 84 of his games in every situation (the TOI and GP columns follow the strength filter). Giveaways are a scorer's judgement: from 2024-25 the league records them consistently; before that the count was largely the rink's scorer, so 2023-24 is adjusted for the rink and is best compared within its season. Blank on the separate rows of a player traded mid-season.",C=" Blank under 100 minutes and on rows that pool seasons.",M=["xgv","gv_vs_exp"],L=e=>null==e||"number"!=typeof e?"-":"".concat(e>0?"+":"").concat(Number.isInteger(e)?String(e):e.toFixed(2)),W=e=>null==e||"number"!=typeof e?"-":"".concat(e>0?"+":"").concat(e.toFixed(2)),U=[{key:"gv",label:"GV",group:"Turnovers",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,strengthAware:!1,toiKey:"xto_toi_seconds",gpKey:"xto_gp",help:{text:"GV = his giveaways: the times the scorer charged him with handing the puck over."+N}},{key:"xgv",label:"xGV",group:"Turnovers",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,strengthAware:!1,toiKey:"xto_toi_seconds",gpKey:"xto_gp",help:{text:"xGV = the giveaways expected from his puck touches, role and where he plays: his attempts, primary assists and takeaways per 60, his share of his unit's attempts, minutes a game, on-ice CF%, power-play and penalty-kill shares, the shifts he gets (zone start, score, period, length, competition, back-to-backs) and the rink's scorer. Forwards and defencemen fitted apart; each season's weights fitted on earlier seasons of the same giveaway recording, except 2024-25, the first season of the new recording, which is fitted on 2025-26. No season's weights come from its own games."+N+C}},{key:"gv_vs_exp",label:"GV vs exp",group:"Turnovers",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,strengthAware:!1,toiKey:"xto_toi_seconds",gpKey:"xto_gp",format:W,help:{text:"GV vs exp = xGV - GV. Positive is good: fewer giveaways than expected. Expected from his puck touches, role and where he plays; heavy puck carriers rank high on giveaways ‚Äî this column credits avoiding them relative to that load. Carries are not in the play-by-play, so the biggest carriers still tend to sit below zero."+N+C}}],X=["pd","pt","pen_diff","xpd","xpt","xpen_diff","pd_vs_exp","pt_vs_exp","pen_vs_exp"],Y="/glossary#penalties",q=" Counted: minors (a double minor once), majors other than fighting, match penalties and penalty shots, whether or not he was on the ice. Fights and misconducts are not counted.",J=" Expected = his minutes \xd7 the same season's league rate for a skater of his position (forward or defenceman), at that strength, home or away, by score and period. No term for role or minutes: depth players take more penalties a minute, and that stays in as part of who they are.",Q=' A count: the rate toggle turns it into Per 60 or Per 84. Follows the strength filter (All, ES, 5v5, PP, PK; a single state such as 5v4 reads "-"), the date window and the season; a delayed call counts at the strength the game was at. Power-play or penalty-kill alone is mostly noise. Regular season, 2023-24 on. Blank on the separate rows of a player traded mid-season.',$=[{key:"pd",label:"PenD",group:"Penalties",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,help:{text:"PenD = penalties drawn: penalties called on an opponent that he drew."+q+Q,href:Y}},{key:"pt",label:"PenT",group:"Penalties",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,help:{text:"PenT = penalties taken: penalties called on him."+q+Q,href:Y}},{key:"pen_diff",label:"Pen+/-",group:"Penalties",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,format:L,help:{text:"Pen+/- = penalties drawn minus penalties taken."+q+Q,href:Y}},{key:"xpd",label:"xPenD",group:"Penalties",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,format:b,help:{text:"xPenD = the penalties drawn expected of a league-average skater in his minutes."+J+Q,href:Y}},{key:"xpt",label:"xPenT",group:"Penalties",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,format:b,help:{text:"xPenT = the penalties taken expected of a league-average skater in his minutes."+J+Q,href:Y}},{key:"xpen_diff",label:"xPen+/-",group:"Penalties",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,format:W,help:{text:"xPen+/- = expected penalties drawn minus taken. Mostly position: forwards draw more than they take, defencemen the reverse."+J+Q,href:Y}},{key:"pd_vs_exp",label:"PenD vs exp",group:"Penalties",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,format:W,help:{text:"PenD vs exp = PenD ‚àí xPenD. Positive is good: more penalties drawn than a league-average skater in his minutes."+J+Q,href:Y}},{key:"pt_vs_exp",label:"PenT vs exp",group:"Penalties",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,format:W,help:{text:"PenT vs exp = xPenT ‚àí PenT, turned around so that positive is good: fewer penalties taken than a league-average skater in his minutes."+J+Q,href:Y}},{key:"pen_vs_exp",label:"Pen+/- vs exp",group:"Penalties",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,format:W,help:{text:"Pen+/- vs exp = PenD vs exp + PenT vs exp: the power plays he gained his team beyond a league-average skater in his minutes. Positive is good."+J+Q,href:Y}}],ee=new Set(["es","5v5"]),et=["xoz_pct","oz_vs_exp","xdz_pct","dz_vs_exp"],es=200,ea=" Expected from three things: how his even-strength shifts started (offensive-, neutral- or defensive-zone faceoff, or on the fly), forward or defenceman, and his team that season, measured from his teammates with him left out. So it is relative to his zone starts, his position and his teammates: an on-ice-relative stat. His linemates' zone time is largely his own, so part of what he does is counted as his team's and the gap understates him. One fit over 2021-22 to 2025-26, weighted by minutes.",eo=" Actual zone time is NHL EDGE tracking, regular season. Even strength only: ES and 5v5 read it "+'(5v5 is EDGE\'s even-strength split), any other strength reads "-". Blank under '.concat(es," ")+"even-strength minutes in the season and on rows that pool seasons. A share: the rate toggle leaves it alone.",ei=[{key:"xoz_pct",label:"xOZ%",group:"Zone time",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"pct",format:b,help:{text:"Expected OZ%: the share of his even-strength on-ice time we would expect in the offensive zone, 0 to 100."+ea+eo}},{key:"oz_vs_exp",label:"OZ% vs exp",group:"Zone time",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"pct",format:b,help:{text:"OZ% vs exp = OZ% - xOZ%, in points. Positive: more offensive-zone time than his starts, his position and his teammates account for. It follows the player when he changes teams (r 0.25 season to season for players who moved), which the raw OZ% hardly does."+eo}},{key:"xdz_pct",label:"xDZ%",group:"Zone time",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"pct",format:b,help:{text:"Expected DZ%: the share of his even-strength on-ice time we would expect in the defensive zone, 0 to 100."+ea+eo}},{key:"dz_vs_exp",label:"DZ% vs exp",group:"Zone time",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"pct",format:b,help:{text:"DZ% vs exp = xDZ% - DZ%, in points, turned around so that positive is good: less defensive-zone time than his starts, his position and his teammates account for (r 0.28 season to season for players who moved)."+eo}}],en="/glossary#luck",el=" Follows the strength, game type and date filters. At All it counts even strength, power play and penalty kill, not empty-net play (empty-net shots carry no xG). Blank under score-and-venue adjustment and on the separate team rows of a player traded mid-season.",er=" Expected goals are scaled to the league's own finishing in the same season and situation, so a league-average finisher reads zero.",eh=" A percentage: the Total / Per 60 / Per 84 toggle leaves it alone.",ed=" A count: the rate toggle turns it into Per 60 or Per 84.",ep=" His assists come off his teammates' goals, so the column moves them by the goals his teammates scored above or below expected, at his own rate of assists per teammate goal. That rate is pulled toward his position's (forward or defenceman) by an amount measured from past seasons of assists, so a short season is mostly the position's rate and a teammate goal count of zero does no harm. His own goals are kept as he scored them; his own finishing is the Own GAx column.",eu=e=>null==e||"number"!=typeof e?"-":"".concat(e>0?"+":"").concat(e.toFixed(1)),eg=[{key:"lk_oish_pct",label:"oiSH%",group:"On ice (PDO)",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"pct",format:b,help:{text:"oiSH% = 100 \xd7 GF \xf7 SF: the share of his team's shots on goal that went in while he was on the ice, his own included."+eh+el,href:en}},{key:"lk_oisv_pct",label:"oiSV%",group:"On ice (PDO)",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"pct",format:b,help:{text:"oiSV% = 100 \xd7 (1 - GA \xf7 SA): the save percentage behind him while he was on the ice."+eh+el,href:en}},{key:"lk_pdo",label:"PDO",group:"On ice (PDO)",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"pct",format:b,help:{text:"PDO = oiSH% + oiSV%. The league sits near 100; well above or below it, the bounces were doing a lot of the work. It mixes his teammates' shooting, his own and his goalie's."+eh+el,href:en}},{key:"lk_tm_sh_pct",label:"Tm SH%",group:"Him removed",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"pct",format:b,help:{text:"Tm SH% = 100 \xd7 (GF - his goals) \xf7 (SF - his shots): his teammates' shooting percentage while he was on the ice, with his own shots and goals taken out."+eh+el,href:en}},{key:"lk_tm_gf",label:"Tm GF",group:"Him removed",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,help:{text:"Tm GF = GF - his goals: the goals his teammates scored while he was on the ice."+ed+el,href:en}},{key:"lk_tm_xgf",label:"Tm xGF",group:"Him removed",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,format:b,help:{text:"Tm xGF = xGF - his iXG, on the raw model with no shooter talent: what his teammates' shots would have scored for league-average finishers."+er+ed+el,href:en}},{key:"lk_tm_gax",label:"Tm GAx",group:"Him removed",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,format:eu,help:{text:"Tm GAx = Tm GF - Tm xGF: his teammates' goals above what league-average finishers would have scored on the same shots."+er+ed+el,href:en}},{key:"lk_tm_dfsh_pct",label:"Tm dFSh%",group:"Him removed",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"pct",format:W,help:{text:"Tm dFSh% = 100 \xd7 Tm GAx \xf7 his teammates' unblocked attempts: their finishing above expected per 100 unblocked shots, the rate version of Tm GAx (xG is counted on unblocked attempts)."+er+eh+el,href:en}},{key:"lk_tm_xgf_sh",label:"Tm xGF(sh)",group:"Him removed",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,format:b,help:{text:"Tm xGF(sh) = xGF(sh) - his iXG(sh): his teammates' expected goals at their own finishing talent."+er+ed+el,href:en}},{key:"lk_tm_gax_sh",label:"Tm GAx(sh)",group:"Him removed",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,format:eu,help:{text:"Tm GAx(sh) = Tm GF - Tm xGF(sh): his teammates' goals above what their own finishing talent predicts. Where Tm GAx is high and this is near zero, his linemates are good shooters, not lucky ones."+er+ed+el,href:en}},{key:"lk_own_gax",label:"Own GAx",group:"His own finishing",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,format:eu,help:{text:"Own GAx = his goals - his iXG on the raw model: his own finishing above a league-average finisher's on the same shots. The other source of luck in his points, and partly skill."+er+ed+el,href:en}},{key:"lk_pts",label:"Pts",group:"Points",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,help:{text:"His points at the strength: the P column."+ed,href:en}},{key:"lk_a1",label:"A1",group:"Points",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,help:{text:"His primary assists (at All, not counting empty-net play)."+ed+el,href:en}},{key:"lk_a2",label:"A2",group:"Points",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,help:{text:"His secondary assists (at All, not counting empty-net play)."+ed+el,href:en}},{key:"lk_xa1",label:"xA1",group:"Points",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,format:b,help:{text:"xA1 = A1 + his primary assists per teammate goal \xd7 (Tm xGF - Tm GF): his primary assists had his teammates finished like the league."+ep+ed+el,href:en}},{key:"lk_xa2",label:"xA2",group:"Points",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,format:b,help:{text:"xA2 = A2 + his secondary assists per teammate goal \xd7 (Tm xGF - Tm GF)."+ep+ed+el,href:en}},{key:"lk_xa",label:"xA",group:"Points",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,format:b,help:{text:"xA = xA1 + xA2: his assists with normal-shooting linemates."+ep+ed+el,href:en}},{key:"lk_xpts",label:"xPts",group:"Points",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,format:b,help:{text:"xPts = Pts - his assists + xA: his points with normal-shooting linemates, league-average finishers on the same shots."+ep+ed+el,href:en}},{key:"lk_pts_diff",label:"xPts - Pts",group:"Points",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,format:eu,help:{text:"xPts - Pts: the points normal-shooting linemates would have given him, minus the points he has. Positive, his teammates' finishing cost him points; negative, it handed him some."+ep+ed+el,href:en}},{key:"lk_xpts_sh",label:"xPts(sh)",group:"Points",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,format:b,help:{text:"xPts(sh): xPts with his teammates at their own finishing talent (xG(sh)) instead of the league's. His points with the luck out and his linemates' real shooting left in."+ep+ed+el,href:en}},{key:"lk_pts_diff_sh",label:"xPts(sh) - Pts",group:"Points",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,format:eu,help:{text:"xPts(sh) - Pts: the points his teammates' luck alone, beyond their real shooting talent, cost him (positive) or gave him (negative)."+ep+ed+el,href:en}}],ef=" A count: the rate toggle turns it into Per 60 or Per 84. Follows the strength filter (his side's strength: a hit he took on the kill counts under PK), the season, the regular season / playoffs choice and the date window. At All it counts every situation, pulled-goalie play included, as G, A and P do.",ec=" A count: the rate toggle turns it into Per 60 or Per 84. Follows the strength filter, the season, the regular season / playoffs choice and the date window, as G, A and P do.",em=' Counted: minors (a double minor once), majors other than fighting, match penalties and penalty shots, whether or not he was on the ice; not fights or misconducts. A count: the rate toggle turns it into Per 60 or Per 84. Regular season, 2023-24 on, so it reads "-" on playoff rows and older seasons; a single state such as 5v4 reads "-" too. The Extras tab sets it beside the league expectation.',e_=[{key:"toi_es_seconds",label:"EV TOI",group:"Identity",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,strengthAware:!1,coverage:"even strength only",kind:"identity",format:e=>(0,o.YQ)(e),help:{text:"Even-strength ice time: 5v5, 4v4 and 3v3, both goalies in. Whatever the strength filter says, like PP TOI and PK TOI."}},{key:"iprimary_assists",label:"A1",group:"Individual",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,help:{text:"A1 = primary assists: the last pass before the goal."+ec}},{key:"iprimary_points",label:"P1",group:"Individual",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,help:{text:"P1 = G + A1: goals and primary assists, the points closest to the goal."+ec}},{key:"individual_cf",label:"iCF",group:"Individual",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,help:{text:"iCF = his shot attempts: goals, shots on goal, misses and blocked attempts (one a teammate blocked included, as Corsi counts it)."+ec}},{key:"iblk",label:"iBLK",group:"Individual",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,help:{text:"iBLK = opponent shots he blocked, as the NHL box score counts them: a teammate's shot hitting him is not a block."+ec}},{key:"ihf",label:"iHF",group:"Individual",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,help:{text:"iHF = hits he made, as the rink's scorer recorded them. Hit counts vary by rink, so compare players across arenas with care."+ef}},{key:"iha",label:"iHA",group:"Individual",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,help:{text:"iHA = hits he took: the times he was the one hit. Often a sign of who carries the puck."+ef}},{key:"pt",label:"PenT",group:"Individual",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,help:{text:"PenT = penalties taken: penalties called on him."+em,href:Y}},{key:"pd",label:"PenD",group:"Individual",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,help:{text:"PenD = penalties drawn: penalties called on an opponent that he drew."+em,href:Y}},{key:"pen_diff",label:"Pen+/-",group:"Individual",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,format:L,help:{text:"Pen+/- = penalties drawn minus penalties taken: the power plays he gave his team, net."+em,href:Y}}],eb=" The four parts add up to Net_RTG: season sums in goals, like Off_RTG and Def_RTG, so at Per 84 they add up to his season Net Rating. Each is measured against the average skater at his position for that part. Whole regular seasons at All situations only: blank under any other strength, a date window, playoffs and on the separate rows of a player traded mid-season. The worked example in the Net Rating writeup itemises every line behind them.",ek=e=>null!=e?e.toFixed(1):"-",ex=[{key:"nr_individual",label:"Individual",group:"Net Rating parts",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,kind:"count",format:ek,help:{text:"Individual: what Net Rating credits him for himself, goals, assists, shots on goal, penalties drawn and taken and blocked shots, at Game Score's weights."+eb,href:"/glossary#net-rating"}},{key:"nr_onice_for",label:"On-ice for",group:"Net Rating parts",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,kind:"count",format:ek,help:{text:"On-ice for: his team's 5v5 xGF(sh) and goals while he was on the ice, against what the league and his team would score in those minutes."+eb,href:"/glossary#net-rating"}},{key:"nr_onice_against",label:"On-ice against",group:"Net Rating parts",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,kind:"count",format:ek,help:{text:"On-ice against: the 5v5 xGA(sh) and goals against while he was on the ice, against what the league and his team would allow in those minutes. Positive is good."+eb,href:"/glossary#net-rating"}},{key:"nr_context",label:"Context",group:"Net Rating parts",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,kind:"count",format:ek,help:{text:"Context: the ice-time pace credit (heavy minutes come at a higher pace against, and he is not charged for it) plus the penalty-kill context term (his shorthanded xGA(sh) against what his starts and minutes predict)."+eb,href:"/glossary#net-rating"}}],ey=" Game Score Plus (GS+): one number for each player's game, in goals, built on Dom Luszczyszyn's Game Score, the game card's number. Regular season only (2023-24 on). Under Even strength, 5v5, Power play and Penalty kill each column is the part of each game's GS+ earned in that state, and the parts, with net-empty play and the credit for killing more penalties than his teammates (both counted only in All situations), add up to the All situations number; any other single state reads \"-\", as do playoff rows and the separate team rows of a player traded mid-season. Pooled seasons add their games; a pool reaching back before 2023-24 reads \"-\".",ew=e=>null==e||"number"!=typeof e?"-":(0,a.Mw)(e),ev=[{key:"gs_plus",label:"GS+",group:"GS+",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"count",gpKey:"gs_plus_gp",toiKey:"gs_plus_toi_seconds",format:ew,help:{text:"GS+ = his GS+ added up over the games, in goals. A count: the rate toggle turns it into Per 60 of his minutes at the filter's strength or Per 84 of his games."+ey,href:"/glossary?tab=writeups&writeup=game-score-plus"}},{key:"gs_plus_pg",label:"GS+/GP",group:"GS+",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"rate",format:ew,help:{text:"GS+/GP = GS+ per game, in goals: the game card's average night, over all his games under every strength filter. The rate toggle leaves it alone."+ey,href:"/glossary?tab=writeups&writeup=game-score-plus"}},{key:"gs_plus_off",label:"GS+ Off",group:"GS+",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"count",gpKey:"gs_plus_gp",toiKey:"gs_plus_toi_seconds",format:ew,help:{text:"GS+ Off = the offensive half of his GS+, in goals: GS+ Off + GS+ Def = GS+ in every game. A count: the rate toggle scales it on GS+'s own games and minutes."+ey,href:"/glossary?tab=writeups&writeup=game-score-plus"}},{key:"gs_plus_def",label:"GS+ Def",group:"GS+",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,kind:"count",gpKey:"gs_plus_gp",toiKey:"gs_plus_toi_seconds",format:ew,help:{text:"GS+ Def = the defensive half of his GS+, in goals: GS+ minus GS+ Off. A count: the rate toggle scales it on GS+'s own games and minutes."+ey,href:"/glossary?tab=writeups&writeup=game-score-plus"}}],eP=(e,t,s)=>({key:e,label:t,group:"GS+ parts",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,kind:"count",gpKey:"gs_plus_gp",toiKey:"gs_plus_toi_seconds",format:ew,help:{text:"".concat(t,": ").concat(s," The eight GS+ parts add up to GS+, in goals. A count: the rate toggle ")+"scales it on GS+'s own games and minutes."+ey,href:"/glossary?tab=writeups&writeup=game-score-plus"}}),eG=[eP("gsp_scoring","Scoring","his goals, primary and secondary assists at Game Score's weights."),eP("gsp_shots","Shots","his shots on goal at Game Score's weight."),eP("gsp_blocks","Blocks","the shots he blocked at Game Score's weight."),eP("gsp_on_ice","On-ice","his 5v5 on-ice differentials, attempts (CF - CA) and goals (GF - GA), at Game Score's weights."),eP("gsp_fo_value","Faceoffs","the goal value of his draws: his prior-season win rate above 50% times what each draw's zone and strength is worth (JP Gambatese's method)."),eP("gsp_xpen","Penalties (exp.)","GS+'s penalty expectation, ePD ‚àí ePT: his minutes at each strength times last season's league rate for his position and his own shrunk rate from last season. Not the penalties he took, and not the xPenD and xPenT on Extras."),eP("gsp_shutdown","Shutdown","credit for hard minutes: the chances against expected from whom he faced and how he was deployed (zone start, score, 5v5 or the kill), measured against his teammates so each team's adds to zero. On the penalty kill, this only compares how tough his kill minutes were with his teammates'. Credit for killing more penalties than them counts under All situations."),eP("gsp_team","Team line","minus his share of his team's five-on-five baseline, which GS+ hands to the team line: below zero on a good team, above it on a bad one. The other seven are the raw terms, which still hold it. It is all five-on-five, so it reads 0 under Power play and Penalty kill.")],eA=" Goals above average, positive is good. Regular season; the strength filter does not change it. Blank on playoff rows, under a date window and on the separate rows of a player traded mid-season.",eV=' A count: the rate toggle scales it on his own games and his 5v5 and 5-on-4 minutes. Pooled seasons add; a pool reaching a season without it reads "-".',eT=" Already per 82 games, so the rate toggle leaves it alone. Blank on rows that pool seasons.",eS=[{key:"value_est",label:"Value",group:"Estimates",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,strengthAware:!1,kind:"count",gpKey:"value_est_gp",toiKey:"value_est_toi_seconds",format:eu,help:{text:"Value Estimate: his goals above average this season, what he did rather than what he will do. Credited for every stretch of play he was on for at 5v5 and at 5-on-4 (power play and penalty kill), offence plus defence. The season is refitted as it goes, so earlier games are revalued as it fills in."+eA+eV}},{key:"eoy_value",label:"EoY Value",group:"Estimates",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,strengthAware:!1,kind:"season",format:eu,help:{text:"EoY Value Forecast: the Value Estimate projected to the end of the season, his value so far plus his expected games left at a rate drawn from his Talent Estimate (with his current team's system) and his value per game so far. The current season only. Slightly conservative: players projected well above or below average have tended to finish about 5% further out."+eA+" A season total, so the rate toggle leaves it alone."}},{key:"talent_est",label:"Talent",group:"Estimates",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!0,strengthAware:!1,kind:"rate",format:eu,help:{text:"Talent Estimate: goals above average per 82 games, what we expect of him from here. Read from this season and the three before it, weighted toward this one, offence plus defence. The latest estimate for the current season, the season-end one for a finished season."+eA+eT}}],ej=[{key:"value_est_off",label:"Value Off",group:"Estimate parts",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,strengthAware:!1,kind:"count",gpKey:"value_est_gp",toiKey:"value_est_toi_seconds",format:eu,help:{text:"Value Estimate, Offence: the goals scored while he was on at 5v5 and on the power play, against what average attackers would score in his place. Value Off + Value Def = Value."+eA+eV}},{key:"value_est_def",label:"Value Def",group:"Estimate parts",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,strengthAware:!1,kind:"count",gpKey:"value_est_gp",toiKey:"value_est_toi_seconds",format:eu,help:{text:"Value Estimate, Defence: the expected goals against, xG(sh), kept out while he was on at 5v5 and on the penalty kill, against average defenders in his place. Value Off + Value Def = Value."+eA+eV}},{key:"talent_est_off",label:"Talent Off",group:"Estimate parts",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,strengthAware:!1,kind:"rate",format:eu,help:{text:"Talent Estimate, Offence: per 82 games, at 5v5 and on the power play. Talent Off + Talent Def = Talent."+eA+eT}},{key:"talent_est_def",label:"Talent Def",group:"Estimate parts",sortable:!0,defaultVisible:!1,strengthAware:!1,kind:"rate",format:eu,help:{text:"Talent Estimate, Defence: per 82 games, at 5v5 and on the penalty kill. Talent Off + Talent Def = Talent."+eA+eT}}],eE=["talent_est","talent_est_off","talent_est_def","eoy_value","talent_est_sd","talent_est_off_sd","talent_est_def_sd"],eF=["value_est","value_est_off","value_est_def","value_est_gp","value_est_toi_seconds"];function eD(e){let t=new Map(e.map(e=>[e.key,e])),s=new Map([...t,...[...e_,...ex,...eS,...ej].map(