 distance since the prior event, whether it was the shooting team's possession, and one-hots for the prior event type. They carry the speed-of-play and possession-context signal that distinguishes a clean sniper's shot from a contested point shot at the same coordinates. Candidates for ‚Äúprior event‚Äù are restricted to on-ice play events ‚Äî coordinate-less types like ",(0,a.jsx)("code",{children:"stoppage"}),", ",(0,a.jsx)("code",{children:"period-end"}),", and"," ",(0,a.jsx)("code",{children:"game-end"})," are excluded, since a goal also generates one of those at its own timestamp and an unfiltered feed let that no-coordinate row become the goal's own predecessor (see Pipeline)."]}),(0,a.jsx)("h3",{className:"font-serif text-xl mt-6 mb-2",children:"Why poke and bat get their own one-hots"}),(0,a.jsxs)("p",{children:["Poke and bat shots get their own one-hot features rather than folding into"," ",(0,a.jsx)("code",{children:"shot_type_other"}),': each has 1,300+ samples and an empirical goal rate of 11‚Äì13%, distinct enough that lumping them into the generic "other" bucket would inflate that baseline and bias every other shot-type coefficient toward it.']}),(0,a.jsx)("p",{children:"Empty-net shots are excluded from the model entirely rather than isolated with their own feature; the reasoning is in the Calibration section."}),(0,a.jsx)("h3",{className:"font-serif text-xl mt-6 mb-2",children:"Tips and deflections at same distance"}),(0,a.jsxs)("p",{children:["Tip-in and deflected shot types score ",(0,a.jsx)("em",{children:"conditional on geometry"}),": controlled for distance and angle, a tipped shot converts less often than a clean wrist shot ‚Äî it is harder to aim. The ",(0,a.jsx)("em",{children:"unconditional"})," goal rate for tips is higher because tips happen closer in. The model decomposes these two effects rather than conflating them."]})]})}let ta=["#cde2fb","#9ec5f4","#6da7ec","#3987e5","#256abf","#184f95","#0d366b"],tn=[.01,.03,.08,.15,.25],to="#14130f