t, and the model tracks that almost exactly. With the net empty it barely falls at all ‚Äî a shot only has to be accurate, not to beat anyone ‚Äî yet the same distance term is applied, so close-range attempts are over-valued and long ones under-valued. One shared coefficient cannot bend two different curves. A few hundred shots a season also cannot support well-calibrated probabilities. Both are listed as limitations rather than fixed."]}),t.per_distance&&t.per_distance.length>0&&(0,a.jsxs)(a.Fragment,{children:[(0,a.jsx)("h3",{className:"font-serif text-xl mt-6 mb-2",children:"Level check by distance"}),(0,a.jsxs)("p",{children:["A different question from the curve above, and a harsher one. That is a held-out reliability curve from the fitted model; this is every scored regular-season shot we hold ‚Äî actual goals over predicted, in five-foot bands. A model can be well calibrated on average and still be wrong in a shape, so the league total (",(t.per_distance.reduce((e,t)=>e+t.goals,0)/t.per_distance.reduce((e,t)=>e+t.xg,0)).toFixed(4),") is the least informative number here. The shape is in the bands below."]}),(0,a.jsxs)("table",{className:"w-full text-sm mt-2 mb-3 border border-rule",children:[(0,a.jsx)("thead",{children:(0,a.jsxs)("tr",{className:"border-b border-rule-strong text-ink-faint text-[11px] tracking-wider",children:[(0,a.jsx)("th",{className:"px-3 py-2 text-left font-medium",children:"Distance"}),(0,a.jsx)("th",{className:"px-3 py-2 text-right font-medium",children:"Shots"}),(0,a.jsx)("th",{className:"px-3 py-2 text-right font-medium",children:"Goals"}),(0,a.jsx)("th",{className:"px-3 py-2 text-right font-medium",children:"Actual / predicted"}),(0,a.jsx)("th",{className:"px-3 py-2 text-right font-medium",children:"z"})]})}),(0,a.jsx)("tbody",{children:t.per_distance.map(e=>{let t=null!==e.z&&Math.abs(e.z)>=3;return(0,a.jsxs)("tr",{className:"border-b border-rule last:border-b-0",children:[(0,a.jsx)("td",{className:"px-3 py-2 font-medium",children:nul