wise correlation of about ",r?sH(r.lineup.implied_pairwise_rho):"‚Ä¶","), and the total's band is widened by that factor rather than printed on an independence assumption."]})]}),(0,a.jsxs)(h.Section,{id:"provenance",title:"Where it comes from, and what checks it",children:[(0,a.jsxs)("p",{children:["The fit is ",(0,a.jsx)("code",{children:"backend/research/nr_forecast_fit.py"}),"; its tables are"," ",(0,a.jsx)("code",{children:"research/nr_forecast/holdout.md"})," and this page's data file. The parameters it chose go to ",(0,a.jsx)("code",{children:"scraper/nr_forecast_params.json"})," with a fingerprint of the ",(0,a.jsx)("code",{children:"compute_net_rating.py"})," they were fitted against, and the stage that writes the table, ",(0,a.jsx)("code",{children:"scraper.compute_net_rating_forecast"}),", refuses to run against a different one. The arithmetic both use is ",(0,a.jsx)("code",{children:"scraper/nr_forecast_lib.py"}),", one implementation, so what was validated is what runs."]}),(0,a.jsxs)("p",{children:["Two checks run on every write: with no games in the season the projection must equal the talent, and with the season complete it must equal the realised mean; the stage raises if either gap is not zero. On the finished 2025‚Äì26 season the stage's year-end number matched ",(0,a.jsx)("code",{children:"player_ratings.net_rating"})," to 4 \xd7 10‚Åª\xb9‚Å∞ on 715 skaters with twenty or more games, which is the identity holding, and the season-start prior for that season missed the realised value by 4.07 per 84 on average (3.97 per 82), in line with the holdout."]}),r&&(0,a.jsxs)("p",{className:"text-sm text-ink-faint",children:["Methods file fitted ",r.fitted_at.slice(0,10),". A full three-season history is worth, in current-season games,"," ",["F_o","F_d","D_o","D_d"].map(e=>{var t;return"".concat(e.replace("_"," \xb7 ")," ").concat(sB(null!=(t=d(e))?t:void 0))}).join(", "),"."]}),null===r&&(0,a.jsx)("p",{className:"text-sm text-ink-faint",children:"The metho