ntage: every game that went past regulation scored as a tie, one point each, the way the standings were kept before the shootout. (2RW + overtime games) / 2GP.","PythPts%":"Pythagorean expectation: goals for to the k divided by the sum of goals for and goals against to the k, on goals excluding shootout goals, with k fitted on every season since 2010-11; moved onto the points scale by adding half of the league's overtime share for each expected loss.","Pyth W%":"The Pythagorean win share itself, before the move onto the points scale.","xW%":"Expected winning percentage: the Pythagorean expectation on expected goals, xGF(sh+sv) to the k over the sum of xGF(sh+sv) and xGA(sh+sv) to the k, with k fitted on every team-season since 2015-16 so that teams which out-chance their opponents at a given rate win as often as the number says. Regulation and overtime chances; no shootouts.","xPts%":"xW% on the points scale, moved there the way PythPts% is: half of the league's overtime share added for each expected loss.",SRS:"Simple Rating System: average goal margin plus average opponent rating, solved so every team's rating is its margin against an average schedule. Goals in regulation and overtime; a shootout is a zero margin. League average 0.",MOV:"Average goal margin per game, shootouts as zero.",SOS:"Strength of schedule: the average rating of the opponents faced (SRS minus MOV).",Elo:"Elo rating, replayed over every regular-season game in the database, carried between seasons toward 1500, with the margin of victory weighting the update and a home-ice term in the expectation. 1500 is average.",Massey:"Massey's least-squares rating (Who's #1?, ch. 2): the goal margins explained by a rating for each team plus one home-ice term. Without the home-ice term it is SRS exactly.","Massey Off / Massey Def":"Massey's split of the rating into an offensive and a defensive part (rating = off + def), each in goals per game against average; higher is better for both.",Colley:"Colley's rating (ch. 3): wins and losses only, Laplace-smoothed, each opponent's rating feeding back into yours. A game past regulation is half a win for each side. League average 0.500.",Keener:"Keener's rating (ch. 4): the share of the goals in each game, smoothed and skewed so a blowout counts little more than a clear win, with the leading eigenvector of that matrix as the rating. League average 1.00.",Markov:"The Markov rating (ch. 6): every team votes for the teams that scored on it, goal by goal, and the rating is where a random walk along those votes spends its time. League average 1.00. Withheld early in a season, while it ranks teams on a handful of results.","OD / OD Off / OD Def":"The offense-defense rating (ch. 7): offence is the goals scored weighted by how hard each opponent is to score on, defence is the goals allowed weighted by how good each opponent is at scoring, solved together. OD = Off / Def. Off above 1 is good; Def BELOW 1 is good.",Consensus:"Mean rank over Elo, SRS, Colley, Keener, Markov and OD; over the other five while Markov is withheld.","Proj PTS":"Projected final points: points so far plus the expected points of every remaining game from the dressed lineups' strengths (the same projection as the team cards). Hover for the 80% band.",L10:"The last ten games: wins, losses, overtime losses.",Strk:"The current streak."},o=["P%","L10","Strk","Proj PTS","RgPts%","PythPts%","Pyth W%","xW%","xPts%","SRS","MOV","SOS","Elo","Massey","Massey Off / Massey Def","Colley","Keener","Markov","OD / OD Off / OD Def","Consensus"]},53549:(e,t,s)=>{"use strict";async function a(e){let t=new AbortController,s=setTimeout(()=>t.abort(),6e3);try{let s=await fetch("/api/v1/data/".concat(e),{signal:t.signal});if(!s.ok)throw Error("API ".concat(s.status));return await s.json()}finally{clearTimeout(s)}}async function n(e){try{return await a(e)}catch(s){let t=await fetch("/data/".concat(e));if(!t.ok)throw Error("HTTP ".concat(t.status));return await t.json()}}s.d(t,{W:()=>n})